# The ending all_will_be_crooked (data/endings/all_will_be_crooked.json): the narration the ending screen plays before its slides. The Vagrant tells it
# afterwards: second person, present tense, one or two sentences a line, no game words. First draft by Claude; Gemini edits it.

~ start
Narrator: The goat skull turns its empty eyes on you and stays dark, and somewhere under the roots a lock gives way.
Narrator: The door in the Crooked Tree swings open, slow as a sunrise, and the Crooked Queen walks out into her Hollow.
Narrator: The moon grins wider than you'd have believed a moon could, and every shadow in Wickermoor Hollow starts to bend.
